{"name":"Tournament Field","hex":"#54836b","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tournament","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["During the Middle Ages, a series of battles and other contests designed to prepare knights for war.","A series of games; either the same game played many times, or a succession of games related by a single theme; played competitively to determine a single winning team or individual."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tournament"},{"term":"field","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A land area free of woodland, cities, and towns; an area of open country.","The open country near or belonging to a town or city."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To intercept or catch (a ball) and play it.","To be the team catching and throwing the ball, as opposed to hitting it."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/field"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tournament","blocks":[{"text":"A tournament is an organized competition involving at least three competitors, all participating in a sport or game, with the only way to exit a winner is as its champion. More specifically, the term may be used in either of two distinct senses:"}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tournament","wikidata":"Q500834"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Round-robin_tournament_10teams_en.png/500px-Round-robin_tournament_10teams_en.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Round-robin_tournament_10teams_en.png/500px-Round-robin_tournament_10teams_en.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Example of a round-robin tournament with ten participating teams: each team plays each other team, over nine days","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARound-robin_tournament_10teams_en.png"}],"sounds":{"tournament":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https